    "q-64217": {
      "dom_id": "step-q64217",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The function $y(t)$ gives the position of a particle at time $t.$ Which of the following equations represents a situation in which the particle is undergoing simple harmonic motion?",
      "worked_solution": "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see that the only equation that represents SHM is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4y=0.\n$$\n\nIn the above case:\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=4\\,⟹\\,\\omega =2\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
